All my checking tools (eval, clone, web_fetch, recall) were unavailable in this pass, so this is from general NixOS knowledge — I've flagged what I couldn't verify.

**The config:**

```nix
{
  services.openssh = {
    enable = true;
    settings = {
      PasswordAuthentication = false;
      KbdInteractiveAuthentication = false;
      PubkeyAuthentication = true;
    };
  };
}
```

- `enable = true` starts the `sshd` service.
- `settings` is passed straight into `sshd_config`, so these are the usual OpenSSH directives: `PasswordAuthentication = false` turns off password logins, `KbdInteractiveAuthentication = false` turns off keyboard-interactive (PAM-style) logins, and `PubkeyAuthentication = true` keeps key logins on (it's the default, but being explicit is nice).

**Make sure your key is registered for the user:**

```nix
users.users.alice.openssh.authorizedKeys.keys = [
  "ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3Nza... alice@laptop"
];
```

**Before you deploy:** make sure you have a working key-based session (or console access) already, so you don't lock yourself out when passwords stop working. If you manage root, consider `settings.PermitRootLogin = "prohibit-password"` as well.

